   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to directing the commissioner of environmental conservation to create gift cards for hunting and fishing licenses",
    "basePrintNo": "S6574",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6574-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §11-0706, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6574\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to directing the commissioner of environmental conservation\nto create gift cards for hunting and fishing licenses\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo require the Commissioner of the Department of Environmental\nConservation (DEC) to promulgate rules and regulations establishing\ngift cards for hunting and fishing licenses in New York State.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 11-0706 to require the Commissioner of the\nDepartment of Environmental Conservation to promulgate rules and\nregulations for the sale of gift cards for New York State hunting and\nfishing licenses.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSection 11-0706 of the Environmental Conservation Law, which was part\nof the 2012-13 New York State Budget, Chapter 58 of the Laws of 2012,\nprovides that the Commissioner is authorized to establish gift cards\nfor hunting and fishing.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill requires the Commissioner of the Department of Environmental\nConservation to promulgate rules and regulations so that gift cards\nfor hunting and fishing can be sold in New York State. Allowing for\nthe purchase of gift cards for such licenses encourages their sale and\nmay increase revenue for the state.\n\nSimilar gift cards are already allowed in the State for camping\npermits and Empire Passports which are used for entrance into New York\nState Parks. Gift cards for camping permits, offered by the Office of\nParks, may be used for anything from golf reservations and greens fees\nto the purchase of firewood or boat rentals, in addition to reserving\ncamping sites. Gift cards for camping as well as the Empire Passport\nare even advertised for sale on the web site for the New York State\nOffice of Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation.\n\nIn 2013, the New York State Department of Environmental Conservation\n(DEC) began to issue their own gift cards that can be used for camping\nat all New York State Department of Environmental Conservation\nFacilities. These gifts cards are similar to those offered by the\nOffice of Parks, but they carry their own restrictions as imposed by\nthe DEC and are only for use at DEC facilities.\n\nThus there is a precedent set within the state, and within the DEC in\nparticular, to allow for the sale of recreational gift cards. Hunting\nand fishing are similar recreational activities and the licenses for\nthese activities should be made available through the purchase of gift\ncards.\n\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nPotential for increased revenue.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
